# Key Press Visualizer Example

Captures keyboard input and visualizes the key state using a `BooleanIndicatorNode`.

## Nodes Used

- `keyPress/capture` — emits captured key name and pressed/released state
- `output/display/boolean` — shows a green circle when a key is pressed, gray when released

## Graph

1. Add a `KeyPressCapture` node (Input → Keyboard)
2. Add a `BooleanIndicator` node (Output → Value)
3. Connect `KeyPressCapture.isPressed` → `BooleanIndicator.value`

## Pre-made Graph

Import `key-press.json` to load the wired graph instantly.

## Build & Run

```bash
cmake --build --preset debug
./build/debug/examples/key-press/KeyPressApp
```

Focus the window and press any key to see the indicator light up.
